{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792349336,"nonce":"PZAdN4Txp977IrqgBVW0+dNFwL8=","message":"Landed in 6ef8474446ea1f8e0e663d78d1a93773848dc3b0. wasi-libc defines the four pthread key functions, but its pthread_key_delete never returns in either runtime (a test library that created and then deleted a key hung under wasmtime, single-threaded and threaded alike), so ash_std now defines pthread_key_create, pthread_key_delete, pthread_setspecific and pthread_getspecific itself: one key table for the process, one value per thread, with unit tests for reuse, per-thread values and exhaustion. Checked with a hand-written side module importing all four, linked against both runtime objects: ash --build refuses it with the old runtime ('imports 4 function(s) this runtime does not define') and accepts it with the new, and it runs. Destructors are recorded and never run. Not done here: a published nightly release of Ash, which needs a separate go-ahead.","files":null}]}